From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Pixel2: USB OTG WiFi, charge switch, PMIC plug detect

GKD Pixel2 (and compatible RK3326S boards) share one Type-C port for OTG
WiFi and charging. Combined fix merging former 005, 017, 022, and 023:

* rk817: PMIC PLUG_IN_STS poll, CHRG_IN reset on replug, keep OTG VBUS at
  boot, OTG plug-IRQ balance, charger plug clears host extcon (DTS:
  rockchip,charger-use-pmic-plug)
* E6: skip otg_switch on fixed USB-A host ports, CHRG_IN init at probe
  (DTS: rocknix,fixed-usb-host-vbus)
* phy: skip self-VBUS DCP false charge icon (DTS: rocknix,skip-host-charger-
  detect), iddig host handoff, clear/release forced iddig for role switch
* dwc2: U-Boot gadget to host handoff, enumeration retry fallback

